# Served by the Workers assets binding. Hashed bundles are immutable; the
# HTML shell and version.json are handled by the Worker (no-store).
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Issue #10: no security headers on any response. This file is applied by
# the Cloudflare assets binding, so it only covers what that binding serves
# directly — the SPA shell (every route under apps/web, plus apps/site's
# /about, /privacy, /terms, copied into the same `dist/` by
# scripts/copy-site.mjs) and static files. Hono-generated responses
# (`/item/:id`'s OG-injected HTML, every `/api/*` JSON response) are NOT
# covered by this file at all — see apps/api/src/middleware/securityHeaders.ts
# for those, wired in apps/api/src/index.ts.
#
# script-src is hash-based, not 'unsafe-inline', for the three inline
# `<script>` tags that actually ship in the exported HTML (confirmed by
# running `expo export` twice and diffing the hashes — both matched a
# byte-for-byte second run, so these are stable, not export-run-dependent):
#   - sha256-VYy8ShHUfzzRt7GXnoWUg8bhL+AVi/uK7Oqzytw8Se4= is
#     apps/web/app/+html.tsx's PREHYDRATION_SCRIPT — the no-flash dark-mode
#     script that must run before hydration, plus (issue #44) the root
#     redirect that sends a first-time visitor from `/` to `/welcome` before
#     anything paints. Folded into the same script/hash rather than a fourth
#     inline tag; see that file's header comment for why the redirect has to
#     run before hydration at all.
#   - sha256-67fhrP0+BkBqmgGGXTtgiVO/9EQs3QruYNU/7fnRkI8= is
#     `globalThis.__EXPO_ROUTER_HYDRATE__=true;`, injected by Expo Router's
#     own static-rendering output, not by any file in this app.
#   - sha256-d6qbtEYff/sB38YyzuzhASbVmmOidU/UFC9mNit47j4= is the equivalent
#     no-flash script inline in apps/site/public/{about,privacy,terms}.html
#     (a different app, not owned by this file's issue, but served from the
#     same dist/ under this same _headers — breaking it would be exactly the
#     "silently breaks theming" failure mode this comment is trying to avoid
#     on the app side). If that script's text ever changes, this hash goes
#     stale silently. That is no longer unguarded (issue #194): preflight's
#     `csp-script-hash` check hashes both of the above from source, asserts
#     each appears in this file AND in securityHeaders.ts, and fails on any
#     'sha256-' either policy declares that matches no script in the tree —
#     so a stale leftover is caught as well as a missing value. What it still
#     cannot do is confirm the browser agrees; that needs a
#     curl/CSP-report-only pass against a live deploy. The middle hash below
#     is Expo's own output and is not in this tree, so the check verifies it
#     against the literal recorded here — agreement between two things we
#     wrote, not evidence Expo still emits it.
# connect-src (issue #132) is the directive this file went to production
# without. Absent, it falls back to default-src 'self', and the browser drops
# every cross-origin fetch before it reaches the network — which is what made
# "Use my location" in the give flow report "Couldn't work out your postcode"
# for everyone, forever, while the mocked unit tests for that code stayed
# green. The two origins are the reverse-geocode providers named in
# apps/web/src/lib/geoReverse.ts's exported REVERSE_GEOCODE_ORIGINS;
# apps/web/test/guards/reverseGeocodeCsp.test.ts fails if this line or
# securityHeaders.ts stops covering one of them. The Google Ads and
# Cloudflare Web Analytics *beacons* are connect-src too and are deliberately
# NOT listed: neither provider is configured in any environment today, and
# whoever enables one has to add its endpoint here or ship a tag that reports
# nothing.
#
# https://challenges.cloudflare.com is Turnstile's script (loaded via a
# dynamically-inserted <script src>, src/ui/Turnstile.web.tsx) and its widget
# iframe (frame-src). https://www.googletagmanager.com and
# https://static.cloudflareinsights.com are consent.js's injectScript() calls
# — the Google Ads tag and the Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, both loaded
# only once the consent gate grants them. Without these two, CSP silently
# drops the <script src> before it reaches the network (e2e/consent.spec.ts
# is what catches it — see apps/api/src/middleware/securityHeaders.ts's
# matching comment, which this file's CSP must stay identical to).
#
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline': react-native-web renders virtually all
# layout as inline `style="..."` attributes on DOM nodes, which CSP's
# style-src (not just style-src-elem) governs — hashing every element's
# style attribute across the whole app isn't practical, and inline CSS is a
# materially smaller injection risk than inline script. The one inline
# `<style>` *block* (+html.tsx's ROOT_CSS) rides on the same allowance.
#
# img-src allows data:/blob: for the give flow's client-side photo previews
# (src/lib/images/pickImages.web.ts sets `photo.objectUrl` from
# `URL.createObjectURL`, rendered as an <ExpoImage source={{uri: ...}}>) and
# expo-image's blurhash placeholder rendering.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none' (plus X-Frame-Options: DENY below, for browsers that
# only honor the older header) stops the give flow and the admin page from
# being framed at all — the concrete risk named in the issue.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.bigdatacloud.net https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'sha256-VYy8ShHUfzzRt7GXnoWUg8bhL+AVi/uK7Oqzytw8Se4=' 'sha256-67fhrP0+BkBqmgGGXTtgiVO/9EQs3QruYNU/7fnRkI8=' 'sha256-d6qbtEYff/sB38YyzuzhASbVmmOidU/UFC9mNit47j4='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
